    "interpretation": "The pinned R580 source gives a conditional route for a foreign tracker into the PMM wait. Migration can merge mapping pushes from multiple accessible GPU IDs into the VA-block tracker; block cleanup can then pass that tracker into the PMM root tracker. The opt-in patch now unlocks the VA block around ordinary no-eviction PMM allocation, retains a successful chunk on the retry list, reacquires the lock, and forces the caller to restart and revalidate. The stock/default allocation path remains unchanged. Thus the specific foreign-tracker wait is statically shown to be unlocked in isolated mode, while the conditional source route still exists. This is not proof of a deadlock or of safe cross-provider completion: PMM wait completion progress and the exact V100+Blackwell registration/runtime path remain unmeasured, and the hybrid frontend still blocks second-provider UVM registration.",
